# 9. SSH Security Aur Man-in-the-Middle Protection

SSH remote servers ko identify karne ke liye **Host Keys** use karta hai.

Jab aap pehli dafa kisi server se connect karte hain to SSH ye message dikha sakta hai:

```text
The authenticity of host 'server2' cannot be established.
```

Is ke saath server ka Host-Key Fingerprint bhi display hota hai.

Example:

```text
ED25519 key fingerprint is SHA256:xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
```

SSH poochta hai:

```text
Are you sure you want to continue connecting (yes/no/[fingerprint])?
```

`yes` type karne se pehle server fingerprint ko kisi trusted source se verify karna chahiye.

---

# Host Key Accept Karne Ke Baad Kya Hota Hai?

Jab aap type karte hain:

```text
yes
```

to Host Key is file mein save ho jati hai:

```text
~/.ssh/known_hosts
```

Future connections mein server ki presented key ko saved key ke saath compare kiya jata hai.

Agar key unexpectedly change ho jaye to SSH ye warning deta hai:

```text
WARNING: REMOTE HOST IDENTIFICATION HAS CHANGED!
```

Is ka matlab ho sakta hai:

- Server reinstall hua hai.
- SSH Host Keys regenerate hui hain.
- IP address ab kisi aur server ko mil gaya hai.
- Man-in-the-Middle attack ho sakta hai.

Reason verify kiye baghair is warning ko ignore nahi karna chahiye.

