# 🔧 Troubleshooting Scenarios

### Scenario 1 – Connection Refused

Error:

```text
ssh: connect to host 192.168.1.67 port 22: Connection refused
```

Server 2 par check karein:

```bash
systemctl status sshd
```

Service start karein:

```bash
sudo systemctl enable --now sshd
```

---

### Scenario 2 – Connection Timed Out

Possible reasons:

- Wrong IP address
- Firewall port 22 block kar raha hai
- Network routing problem
- Server powered off hai
- SSH doosre port par listen kar raha hai

Check karein:

```bash
ping -c 4 192.168.1.67
```

```bash
nc -zv 192.168.1.67 22
```

---

### Scenario 3 – Permission Denied

Error:

```text
Permission denied, please try again.
```

Possible causes:

- Wrong username
- Wrong password
- User remote server par exist nahi karta
- Password authentication disabled hai
- Account locked hai
- SSH configuration user ko deny kar rahi hai

Check karein:

```bash
id myuser1
```

```bash
sudo passwd -S myuser1
```

```bash
sudo journalctl -u sshd -n 50
```

---

### Scenario 4 – Hostname Resolve Nahi Ho Raha

Error:

```text
ssh: Could not resolve hostname server2
```

IP address use karein:

```bash
ssh myuser1@192.168.1.67
```

Ya DNS ya `/etc/hosts` fix karein.

---

### Scenario 5 – Host Key Change Ho Gayi

Error:

```text
WARNING: REMOTE HOST IDENTIFICATION HAS CHANGED!
```

Saved key ko foran remove na karein.

Pehle verify karein ke Host Key kyun change hui.

Change legitimate confirm hone ke baad:

```bash
ssh-keygen -R 192.168.1.67
```

Phir reconnect karein aur new fingerprint verify karein.

---

### Scenario 6 – Firewall SSH Block Kar Raha Hai

Check karein:

```bash
sudo firewall-cmd --list-services
```

SSH allow karein:

```bash
sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --add-service=ssh
sudo firewall-cmd --reload
```

---

### Scenario 7 – SSH Different Port Use Kar Raha Hai

Connect karein:

```bash
ssh -p PORT username@server
```

Example:

```bash
ssh -p 2222 myuser1@192.168.1.67
```

