# 📖 Key Takeaways

- OpenSSH ek software collection hai jo SSH Protocol implement karta hai.
- SSH secure aur encrypted remote communication provide karta hai.
- SSH ka default port `22` hai.
- SSH, Telnet aur traditional FTP se zyada secure hai.
- Agar username specify na kiya jaye to SSH current local username use karta hai.
- Different user se connect karne ke liye `ssh user@server` use karein.
- SSH Host Keys unexpected server identity changes detect karne mein madad karti hain.
- `w`, `whoami`, `hostname` aur `pwd` remote session verify karne mein useful hain.
- SSH server service ka naam `sshd` hai.
- Host-Key warning ko correct reason verify kiye baghair ignore na karein.

